# suite TFXCONV
ok 1 - USD 1,250.00 at 1.25 per GBP is GBP 1,000.00
ok 2 - EUR 1,150.00 at 1.15 per GBP is GBP 1,000.00
ok 3 - GBP 1,000.00 at 1.15 per GBP is EUR 1,150.00
ok 4 - an awkward rate rounds once to the penny
ok 5 - the residual is reported, not hidden in the amount
ok 6 - twelve decimals are kept before rounding
ok 7 - GBP to GBP passes through at a rate of one
ok 8 - the rate is reported with its direction in words
ok 9 - a six decimal conversion is available
ok 10 - a reversed quotation is refused by default
ok 11 - a reversed quotation is turned round on request
ok 12 - both quotations are retained after inversion
ok 13 - the inversion is reported as a warning
ok 14 - a receivable settling at a weaker rate makes a loss
ok 15 - both sterling legs are reported
ok 16 - the same movement on a payable is a gain
ok 17 - no movement realises nothing
ok 18 - a settlement rate of zero is rejected
ok 19 - a missing rate is not parity (FX0001)
ok 20 - the amount is left alone when the rate is missing
ok 21 - a negative rate is rejected (FX0002)
ok 22 - a blank currency is rejected (FX0005)
ok 23 - too many decimal places is rejected (FX0006)
ok 24 - an invalid rate date is rejected (FX0007)
ok 25 - an unknown function is rejected (FX0010)
1..25
# TFXCONV passed 00025 failed 00000
# exit 0
